{"name":"April Wedding","hex":"#c5cfb1","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wedding","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A marriage ceremony; a ritual officially celebrating the beginning of a marriage.","The joining of two or more parts."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of wed"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wedding"}],"entries":[{"title":"April","blocks":[{"text":"April is the fourth month of the year in the Gregorian and Julian calendars. Its length is 30 days."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April"},{"title":"Wedding","blocks":[{"text":"A wedding is a ceremony in which two people are united in marriage. Wedding traditions and customs vary greatly between cultures, ethnicities, races, religions, denominations, countries, social classes, and sexual orientations. Most wedding ceremonies involve an exchange of marriage vows by a couple; a presentation of a gift ; and a public proclamation of marriage by an authority figure or celebrant. Special wedding garments are often worn, and the ceremony is sometimes followed by a wedding reception. Music, poetry, prayers, or readings from religious texts or literature are also commonly incorporated into the ceremony, as well as superstitious customs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Hindu_wedding_rituals_b_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Hindu_wedding_rituals_b_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wedding"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Breviarium_Grimani_-_April.jpg/500px-Breviarium_Grimani_-_April.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Breviarium_Grimani_-_April.jpg/500px-Breviarium_Grimani_-_April.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","